Again, there is another particular and remarkable Text, which you do not repeat but only just refer to, and that is, 1 Corv. v. 11 and according to your own Sense of this Text, it relates to the Lord's Supper: And you tell us, that those profest Christians, who in Justin Martyr's * Time brought a publick Dif grace upon Religion, and were debarr'd, not only from the Eucharist, but from all other Part of the common Worship of Christians; nay, from the common intercourses of Society, were debarr'd, according to St. Paul's Rule, in this Place; which Rule, tho' you do not give us, is this;
